-- facts/cleanliness.rofl — THE DECLARATIONS. Hand-written, never generated.
--
-- This file is to `rules/cleanliness.rofl` what `layer(L)` is to the JS model:
-- the part the OWNER declares and an executor may not. Three vocabularies and
-- one register, and the reason each is closed is the same — a queue that an
-- executor can empty by widening its own vocabulary is not a queue.
--
--   role_decl(R)             what an artifact may BE here
--   duty_decl(R, D)          what a role OWES to earn its place
--   waived_cell(P, D, Why)   a named exemption, with a reason from the list
--   cell_owner(P, D, W)      who is doing it — a work item id
--
-- PROPOSED 2026-09-10 AND NOT YET AUTHORISED. Every row below is a proposal
-- from the session that built the table; `layer(L)` in the JS model is the
-- owner's alone and this is the same kind of declaration. Read the numbers the
-- table produces first, then keep, cut or rename.

-- ==================================================================== ROLES
-- Thirteen, and the test asserts they COVER the tree — an artifact with no
-- role is `roleless[audit]`, which is the `vocabulary_gap` of this table.
role_decl(kernel).       -- src/            the engine
role_decl(semantics).    -- boot/policy/safety.rofl, the engine carried as data
role_decl(port).         -- rust/, adapters/
role_decl(scanner).      -- scanners/       turns something into facts
role_decl(rule_pack).    -- rules/          the reasoning
role_decl(runtime).      -- runtime/        renders, admits, schedules
role_decl(data).         -- facts/          packs and ledgers
role_decl(demo).         -- examples/       exercises a capability
role_decl(gate).         -- test/, scripts/ refuses something
role_decl(measurement).  -- bench/          measures, never refuses
role_decl(document).     -- docs/, *.md
role_decl(skill).        -- skills/         the user-facing surface
role_decl(script).       -- npm run <name>

-- ==================================================================== DUTIES
-- START DELIBERATELY SMALL. Four duties over five roles is enough to find out
-- whether the instrument works; a table that opens two hundred cells on its
-- first run is a table nobody reads. Widen it after the first pass, and widen
-- it on evidence — a duty is worth adding when something rotted for want of it.

-- EVERY artifact owes a consumer. Nothing can reach it => it is dead weight.
-- Applied first to the roles where the answer is unambiguous; `document` and
-- `demo` are deliberately NOT here on the first pass, because a document is
-- reached by being read by a person and this model cannot see that.
duty_decl(kernel, has_consumer).
duty_decl(scanner, has_consumer).
duty_decl(runtime, has_consumer).
duty_decl(rule_pack, has_consumer).

-- A GATE THE REFEREE DOES NOT RUN runs when somebody remembers.
duty_decl(gate, run_by_ci).
duty_decl(script, run_by_ci).

-- A GENERATED PACK WITH NO COMPARE-AND-FAIL GATE cannot go stale loudly.
-- Paid for by facts/rule-shape.rofl: 4 903 lines of drift, nothing red.
duty_decl(data, regenerable).

-- A SCANNER WHOSE FACTS NO RULE PACK READS IS A REPORT WITH EXTRA STEPS.
-- CLAUDE.md says exactly this and nothing checked it until now.
duty_decl(scanner, read_by_rules).

-- A DOCUMENT NOTHING INDEXES is one nobody finds. Seven of nineteen were in
-- that state on 2026-09-10 and `the-target.md` — which says what the whole
-- branch is instrumental to — was one of them.
duty_decl(document, indexed).

-- ================================================================== WAIVERS
-- A CLOSED LIST OF REASONS, defined BEFORE any cell is classified, because
-- `kept` turns the alarm green as effectively as the work and costs a tenth as
-- much — docs/comment-migration-brief.md says so about its own remedy, and the
-- author of that brief admits doing it in the same session.
--
-- Reasons, and nothing else may be used:
--   entry_point            a human runs it; nothing in the tree should reach it
--   owner_decision         the owner has ruled on this cell by name
--   superseded_by_work     a work item will remove the artifact entirely
--
-- EMPTY ON PURPOSE ON THE FIRST PASS. Every waiver here should be a decision
-- somebody made after reading the number, not a way of getting the first run
-- to look clean.

-- ================================================================== OWNERS
-- `cell_owner(Path, Duty, WorkItem)` — an open cell with an owner is
-- scheduled; one without is `unowned[audit]`, and that is what CI refuses.
-- Also empty on the first pass: nothing has been assigned yet, so the first
-- run's `unowned` count IS the backlog this table was built to produce.

-- =================================================================== RATCHET
-- THE QUEUE MAY NOT GROW. A count over a growing tree measures the tree, so
-- this is not a pin on the queue's size — it is a CEILING that only ever comes
-- down, which is a claim about the WORK rather than about the corpus. It also
-- merges: two branches lowering it conflict visibly, where two branches moving
-- a count both stay green and agree on a wrong third number.
--
-- 117 on 2026-09-10. It was 127 an hour earlier and came down by ten without
-- anybody cleaning anything: `scanners/cleanliness_report.ts` and
-- `test/cleanliness.test.ts` gave ten artifacts consumers they did not have.
-- THAT IS THE RATCHET WORKING AND IT IS ALSO ITS LIMIT — the queue shrinks
-- when the tree is wired up as much as when it is cleaned, so the ceiling
-- measures reachability and not virtue. Banked anyway: a ceiling that is not
-- lowered when the number falls stops binding.
--
-- Decomposed so the next reader knows what they are lowering:
--   run_by_ci      89   npm scripts and gates the referee never runs
--   has_consumer   28   part real orphans, part loaded by a runtime-built path
--   read_by_rules   6   a scanner whose facts no rule pack reads
--   indexed         3   CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md, LIMITS.md — README links none
--   regenerable     1   facts/ledger-census.rofl has no compare-and-fail gate
--
-- LOWER IT WHEN WORK LANDS. Raising it is a decision that must say why.
queue_ceiling(120).
